1. Start
2. Read the number of vertices n
3. Read the adjacency matrix elements of size n x n
4. Read the starting vertex start
5. Initialize visited array of size n with all 0s
6. Initialize queue pointers: front = 0, rear = -1
7. Mark starting vertex as visited: visited[start] = 1
8. Insert start into queue:
       rear = rear + 1
       queue[rear] = start
9. Repeat steps 10 to 13 while queue is not empty (front <= rear):
10.    Remove vertex u from front of queue:
           u = queue[front]
           front = front + 1
11.    Print u
12.    For each vertex v from 0 to n - 1:
           If adj[u][v] == 1 and visited[v] == 0 then:
               visited[v] = 1
               rear = rear + 1
               queue[rear] = v
13. Stop
